            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+object"} spectrum object
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
            whose first page consists of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofibers"} homotopy cofibers
            of the filtering and which under suitable conditions converges to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the total object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is a generalization of the traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
            to which it reduces for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+chain+complexes"} (∞,1)-category of chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presented
            in the projective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "spectral+sequence#Examples"} spectral sequence – Examples
          %p
            Moreover, by applying general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-categorical
            notion to naturally arising towers (such as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+tower"} chromatic tower
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+spectral+sequence"} chromatic spectral sequence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} coskeleton
            tower of a dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} E-∞ algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            it naturally produces the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
            below.
          %p
            Therefore in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            one finds a lucky coincidence of historical terminology:
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequences"} spectral sequences
                are essentially
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+diagram"} sequences
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %p The general construction can be summarized as follows:
