                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              While historically the appearances of the root “spectr-” in “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"}> spectral sequence
              ” and in “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"}> spectrum
              ” (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"}> stable homotopy types
              ) are unrelated, prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExistenceOfTheSpectralSequence"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConvergenceOfTheSpectralSequence"}
              say that there is a lucky coincidence of terminology:
            %p
              %em> Every sequence of spectra manifests itself on homotopy groups in a spectral sequence
              \.
            %p
              Moreover, the discussion below in
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
              shows that also conversely, essentially every spectral sequence that appears in practice comes from a sequence of spectra this way.
            %p
              (See also the title of (
              %a{:href => "#Wilson13"}> Wilson 13
              )).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              The spectral sequence above itself only actually depends to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(\mathcal{C})
              = succeed "-functorial" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %h3#SpectralSequenceOfACofilteredObject Spectral sequence of a cofiltered object
          %p We discuss here the dual notion to the spectral sequence of a filtered object above, now for a cofiltered object.
          %blockquote
            %p The following does not just dualize but also change the indexing convention on top of dualization. Needs further discussion/harmonization.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Consider the inclusion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{Z}, \leq)
                    \\to
                    (\mathbb{Z}\cup \{\infty\}, \leq)^{\Delta[1]}
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    n \mapsto (n,\infty)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
